// CROWN — latency rides a TUPLE piped into a two-parameter stage:
// `(loud, 1) |> f` where `f(g, n) = g() + n`, under `with !E`.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Refuses through the pinned boot. The guard on the spread: the parameter
// pairing swaps its sides to decompose the tuple, and a flow that does not
// flip with the swap runs the parameters into the datum.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn loud() = op()
fn f(g, n) = g() + n
fn bad() with !E = (loud, 1) |> f
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
